#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:11
#: 4161a391f52f4739b77c67b955f960fe
msgid "ArduPilot includes a simple \"tin can\" shaped fence centered on home that will attempt to stop your copter/rover from flying/driving too far away by stopping at the fence in some Copter/Rover modes if :ref:`common-object-avoidance-landing-page` is setup."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:13
#: 50e4725542684128977e8711e933d499
msgid "The maximum circular distance and altitude (altitude used by Plane and Copter only) and the vehicle behavior when the fence is reached can be configured using a ground station like Mission Planner or QGC."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:15
#: 7e413f29e9d5472cbe5bea9ce45e77b1
msgid "See :ref:`common-geofencing-landing-page` for fence setup parameters common to all fences. Setup specific to the Cylindrical fence is below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:18
#: d6d06d18b2844b39b3e1d4d2b5bd052f
msgid "Enabling the Cylindrical Fence in Mission Planner"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:20
#: 98f5ebf6df6e40a3a35b905dc40553d5
msgid "To enable Fences, go to the Mission Planner full parameter list (CONFIG->Full Parameter Tree), search for items with ``FENCE_``:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:26
#: 2c513f1ab83f4fd3bc273cbd77ed97aa
msgid "Parameter associated with Cylindrical Fence"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:27
#: 4f0fdb9bb69a442b9284a89784b19f5c
msgid "Set :ref:`FENCE_TYPE<FENCE_TYPE>` bit 1 to \"1\"(+ 2 to value)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:28
#: 98f11928810b402fb9437c5e1f82b694
msgid "Set :ref:`FENCE_RADIUS<FENCE_RADIUS>` to the maximum distance from HOME you want (in meters). This should normally be at least 50m. This value must be larger than :ref:`FENCE_MARGIN<FENCE_MARGIN>` and greater than 30m."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:30
#: 29090a49fdfd4c92becceacdfea59b9d
msgid "Polygon :ref:`FENCE_TYPE<FENCE_TYPE>` fences includes circular fences, as well as polygonal shapes, as specified in the Inclusion/Exclusion fence list. This simple home centered \"TINCAN\" fence is a separate fence. Rover ignores altitudes, if set."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:36
#: 4d56603ca24340b8a13ad73ec9d5659b
msgid "Copter GeoFence Tab"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:38
#: 089091ac4d4a4b0c9ac4e8f275bc0d4e
msgid "Copter and Traditional Heli , when connected to Mission Planner, present a CONFIG tab called GeoFence which provides another way to access these parameters in those vehicles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:44
#: 903c100cf21d4ec493e43c634be01ac8
msgid "Warnings:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:46
#: d471ba34f93c40c8b8176dfac50a7f03
msgid "The minimum recommended cylindrical fence radius is 30m"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:47
#: c18627b114644b08ad2c63072b3600e7
msgid "The fence requires the GPS to be functioning well so do not disable the :ref:`GPS arming check <common-prearm-safety-checks>` nor the :ref:`EKF failsafe <ekf-inav-failsafe>` while the fence is enabled. Conversely, if you disable either of these checks, disable the Fence."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:48
#: ac7844ff4c674fae9d19bb0841cb62d1
msgid "For the best results, ensure RTL is working on your vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:49
#: 13af280a3dce4e15bfa7e4b41e347b68
msgid "With the Fence enabled in Copter and Rover, the pre-arm checks will require you have GPS lock before arming the vehicle."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:51
#: b1a78ae75b534c91999dc8fe18b296b0
msgid "In Copter, if EKF failsafe occurs and the Fence is enabled and you lose GPS lock while flying the fence will be disabled."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:53
#: 2b1b320382cd4c15adb94bb4018f0d50
msgid "In Copter, if EKF failsafe occurs and the Fence is enabled and in an autonomous mode, the vehicle will switch to LAND (HOLD for Rover) because we no longer know the vehicle position and we want to ensure the vehicle never travels far outside the fence. If this is not desired, the pilot can retake control by moving the flight mode switch to a manual mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/common-ac2_simple_geofence.rst:57
#: 61c054d925554ac98ed8259592717a92
msgid "The Copter and Rover backup fences are created 20m out from the previous breached fence not 20m out from the vehicle's position.  This means if you choose to override the fence you may have less than 20m to regain vehicle control before the fence switches the vehicle to the :ref:`FENCE_ACTION<FENCE_ACTION>` again.  If you really want to override the fence, you should be ready to switch the flight mode twice or alternatively set-up the enable/disable fence switch."
msgstr ""

